<title>RUSSIA: Donaldson Lufkin to open Moscow office.</title>
<headline>Donaldson Lufkin to open Moscow office.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. investment bank Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette (DLJ) will open a Moscow office by the end of the year, company founder and Senior Advisor William Donaldson told a news conference on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;This will be more of an investment bank/merchant bank as opposed to a brokerage operation,&quot; he said, adding that the company would work with Russian companies seeking new capital.</p>
<p>He said DLJ officials had visited natural gas monopoly Gazprom  and oil producer as well as other companies on a current trip to Russia.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
